<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indonesian National Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1947">1947</a>–<a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Police Actions</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Indonesian National Revolution was the armed and diplomatic struggle for independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rule, fought from 1947 to 1949 in its main phase. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> launched two major military offensives, known as the Police Actions, but faced international pressure. The conflict ended with Dutch recognition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence">Indonesian independence</a> and the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indonesian-national-revolution.jpg" alt="Indonesian National Revolution" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frans Mendur (also Frans Mendoer) (1913 – 1971) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indonesia_declaration_of_independence_17_August_1945.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
